WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.775
Try it.

2
00:00:00.775 --> 00:00:04.625
Part A of Lab 1 runs in the
kit's folder against fixtures.

3
00:00:04.625 --> 00:00:08.838
Step one proves every call is
declared: nine tests pass.

4
00:00:08.838 --> 00:00:12.581
Step two lists what the re-read
client needs on ServiceNow:

5
00:00:12.581 --> 00:00:16.558
a client-credentials token, then
read and write on the finding

6
00:00:16.558 --> 00:00:20.613
table and create on attachments,
all from one role, the verifier.

7
00:00:20.613 --> 00:00:26.488
Step three is the classic mistake: an
administrator gave the verifier itil as well.

8
00:00:26.488 --> 00:00:30.199
The tool lists the calls,
then reports nothing missing,

9
00:00:30.199 --> 00:00:33.251
itil extra, and least
privilege does not hold.

10
00:00:33.251 --> 00:00:34.375
It exits one.

11
00:00:34.375 --> 00:00:38.776
Step four catches the evidence
export reusing the verifier's role:

12
00:00:38.776 --> 00:00:42.537
the evidence reader is missing
and the verifier is extra.

13
00:00:42.537 --> 00:00:46.476
With the verifier's role, the
export could also close findings.

14
00:00:46.476 --> 00:00:51.290
Step five reruns the original
ServiceNow client tests: seven pass.
